-- ---------------------------------------------------------------- the hop's gravitational factor
-- Contracted against the fermion's σ_k (τ = −iσ/2), ε_ijk tr(σ_i A_m) tr(σ_j A_n)(σ_k)_cd with A = √V − M is
--   Φ_cd(m,n) = 4(M_m M_n)_cd − 2 tr M_m (M_n)_cd − 2 (M_m)_cd tr M_n + (2 tr M_m tr M_n − 2 tr(M_m M_n)) δ_cd
-- (the V and bare √V terms cancel), operators in that order. In the hop it acts after H_p, which leaves the vertex
-- holding one open leg (H_p's index at v); d contracts with that leg, c is the open leg the vertex holds after: the
-- fermion's. Every term has two √V, so it is a root-sum term: source the vertex's states, stage 1 and stage 2 the
-- vertices where the two √V act, target the vertex holding the fermion. The five kinds of term, by their maps:
--   1  4(M_m M_n):         E_n, contract | F̃_n, E_m, contract | F̃_m
--   2  −2 tr M_m (M_n):    E_n, contract | F̃_n, E_m          | R_m
--   3  −2 (M_m) tr M_n:    E_n            | R_n, E_m, contract | F̃_m
--   4  2 tr M_m tr M_n:    E_n            | R_n, E_m          | R_m
--   5  −2 tr(M_m M_n):     E_n            | F̃_n, E_m, contract | R_m
sp-ds : Bool → Nat → List Nat → List Nat
sp-ds s e ds = if s then ds-plus e ds else ds-minus e ds
